# Text files are stored and checked out with LF. Without this, a CSV written by Python's csv.writer
# (which defaults to \r\n) lands in the repository with CRLF, and a shell script that reads such a
# file leaves a stray CR inside the field it read — which is how a published evidence file came to
# parse as 60 half-records instead of 30 whole ones.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
